  "reason": "The existing evidence shows that multimodal models with scvi_n200 RNA encoder, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion (e.g., config_025) achieve the highest accuracy (0.724989). This experiment tests whether using resnet50 as the image encoder (instead of imagenet_vit_l) with the same transformer aggregation and weighted fusion could yield comparable or better performance. It clarifies the impact of image encoder choice while maintaining the promising architecture of the top-performing model. The expected cost is similar to config_025 (3.60 GPU hours), making it a cost-effective way to explore a critical design choice."
